          "mainEntity": [
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "What is a Turnover Certificate for Current Account?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "A formal document issued by a practicing Chartered Accountant certifying the total annual turnover of your business, submitted to a bank as proof of financial activity when opening or upgrading a current account. It must carry a UDIN and is based on your GST returns or income tax returns."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Is GST registration mandatory to open a current account?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "No. Businesses below the GST threshold (Rs 40 lakh for goods, Rs 20 lakh for services) can submit a CA-issued Turnover Certificate instead. Banks accept this as valid proof of business activity under their board-approved KYC policies aligned with RBI guidelines."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Who can issue a Turnover Certificate for Current Account?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Only a practicing Chartered Accountant (CA) holding a full-time Certificate of Practice from ICAI. The certificate must include the CA firm name, Firm Registration Number (FRN), membership number, and a valid UDIN. Certificates without UDIN are invalid and will be rejected."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "What is UDIN and why is it mandatory?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "UDIN (Unique Document Identification Number) is an 18-digit code generated by the CA on the ICAI portal (udin.icai.org) for every certificate. Mandatory since 1 February 2019, it allows banks and regulators to instantly verify that the certificate is genuine and was issued by a qualified, practicing CA."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "How long does it take?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Standard certificates are ready within 24 hours of receiving complete documents. Express service delivers in 6 hours. The digital signed copy is emailed immediately upon UDIN generation. Physical delivery by courier takes 2-4 business days."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "What is the fee?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Patron Accounting charges starting at Rs 1,499 for a standard single-year certificate with UDIN and digital delivery. Multi-year certificates are Rs 2,499. Express (6-hour) service is Rs 2,999. All fees include CA verification, UDIN generation, and digital delivery. Quick Answers Who needs this certificate? Sole proprietors, MSMEs, and freelancers below the GST threshold (Rs 40 lakh) who need to open a current account without GST registration. Is it accepted by all banks? Yes - all scheduled commercial banks in India accept UDIN-verified CA certificates under their KYC policies. Can Patron send it physically? Yes - signed physical copies couriered pan-India within 2-4 business days. How is turnover calculated? Total gross revenue for the financial year (April 1 to March 31), taken from GSTR-1/3B (if GST registered) or ITR P&L account."
              }
